-rise': '#ffcc00',\n","    'LCZ 8 - Large low-rise': '#999999',\n","    'LCZ 9 - Sparsely built': '#ffff99',\n","    'LCZ G - Water': '#0066ff',\n","    'A/B - Dense/scattered trees': '#006600',\n","    'D - Low plants (agricole/naturel)': '#99cc66',\n","    'E - Bare rock/paved': '#cccccc'\n","}\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 12))\n","\n","# Iterate through each LCZ class and plot it with its assigned color\n","for classe, couleur in couleurs_lcz.items():\n","    subset = grille_finale[grille_finale['LCZ'] == classe]\n","    if not subset.empty:\n","        subset.plot(ax=ax, color=couleur, label=classe, edgecolor='none')\n","\n","ax.set_title(\"Carte des classes LCZ avec températures (30m) - Aix-en-Provence\")\n","ax.legend(loc='upper left', bbox_to_anchor=(1, 1), fontsize=8)\n","ax.set_axis_off()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig('/content/drive/MyDrive/UHI_AIX/map_LCZ_temperature_30m.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"Map of LCZ classes with temperature distribution saved.\")"],"execution_count":57,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x1200 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Map of LCZ classes with temperature distribution saved.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"d66cb576"},"source":["### Map Explanations:\n","\n","*   **Observed LST Map**: This map displays the actual Land Surface Temperature (`lst_moyenne`) derived directly from the satellite imagery (Landsat data). It shows the raw temperature values across the study area.\n","    *   **Colormap**: `turbo` is used to represent the temperature gradient, which is a perceptually uniform colormap that helps in distinguishing temperature variations.\n","\n","*   **Modeled LST Map**: This map shows the Land Surface Temperature (`LST_modeled`) predicted by the statistical model (OLS regression) based on the morphological indicators (e.g., fraction of built-up area, vegetation, building height, roughness). It represents the LST as explained by the physical characteristics of the urban environment.\n","    *   **Colormap**: `inferno` is used here, another perceptually uniform colormap, which is good for highlighting temperature differences.\n","\n","*   **Regression Residuals Map**: This map illustrates the difference between the observed LST and the modeled LST (`residuals = lst_moyenne - LST_modeled`). Positive residuals indicate areas where the observed temperature is higher than predicted by the model, while negative residuals indicate areas where it's lower. These differences can point to uncaptured factors or local variations.\n","    *   **Colormap**: `RdYlBu_r` (Red-Yellow-Blue reversed) is a diverging colormap suitable for residuals, where red typically indicates positive values (observed warmer than modeled) and blue indicates negative values (observed cooler than modeled), with yellow/green around zero.\n","\n","All maps are saved as PNG files in the specified `/content/drive/MyDrive/UHI_AIX/` directory."]}],"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[{"file_id":"/v2/external/notebooks/intro.ipynb","timestamp":1787622137213}]},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}